 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 517583,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2218ec51ce9a238f.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Stephen J. Falchek , MD/MERCK Manual)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows a condition called spina bifida. This condition occurs when the neural tube does not close properly at the lower end of the body at the spine. The bottom right condition, called meningomyelocele, is the most severe version of spina bifida. It causes severe impairment, while other versions of the condition may not cause severe impairment.</p>\n<p>Make a claim about why meningomyelocele causes severe impairment.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1011970,
     "content_html": "In meningomyelocele, the sac filled with the cerebrospinal fluid is larger."
    },
    {
     "id": 1011971,
     "content_html": "In meningomyelocele, the brain tissue is also effected."
    },
    {
     "id": 1011972,
     "content_html": "In meningomyelocele, the vertebra housing the spinal cord are weaker."
    },
    {
     "id": 1011973,
     "content_html": "In meningomyelocele, the spinal cord is not in its normal location."
    }
   ],
